<title>DENMARK: Danish March current account deficit 1.3 bln Dkk.</title>
<headline>Danish March current account deficit 1.3 bln Dkk.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Denmark's current account swung into a 1.3 billion crown deficit in March 1997 from a revised 3.1 billion crowns surplus in February, the national statistics office said on Wednesday.  </p>
<p>DANISH CURRENT ACCOUNT (billions of crowns)</p>
<p>	    March 1997     Feb 1997	 March 1996</p>
<p>		-1.3	    +3.1 (2.9)*    +1.1 (+0.1)*</p>
<p>*Revised (original figures in brackets)</p>
<p>Cumulative figures for the past three, six and 12 month periods as per end-March:</p>
<p>(Billions of crowns)  Three-month Six-month Twelve-month</p>
<p>Current account		+5.9	   -1.1	+9.7</p>
<p>Goods			   +10.6	  +20.5	+41.4</p>
<p>Services			 -0.8	   -1.0	 +6.0</p>
<p>Interest, other		-3.9	  -20.6	-37.7</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures are subject to rounding. Market analysts polled by Reuters had predicted an average March current account deficit of 0.6 billion crowns.</p>
<p>--Chris Follett, Copenhagen newsroom +45-33-969652</p>
